    "container": true,
    "reason": "configure (a shell script) and cmake configure run project scripts and write zconf.h into the build folder; Daodan runs builds only in a container"
  },
  "traps": [
    "two primary builds of the same library at the root: CMakeLists.txt (targets zlib, zlibstatic, example, minigzip, example64, minigzip64) and configure + Makefile.in (libz.a, libz.so.1.3.1 and test programs, including infcover that CMake does not build); the root Makefile is only a stub that asks to run ./configure",
    "under CMake the shared and the static library compile the same 15 sources, and example64 and minigzip64 exist only when HAVE_OFF64_T is found; under configure the test programs link the static library, the *sh variants the shared one",
    "CMake renames a zconf.h found in the source folder to zconf.h.included and writes zconf.h into the build folder from zconf.h.cmakein: the header the build uses is generated, which is why build is an include folder",
    "contrib/ and examples/ are not compiled by either primary build: contrib/blast, puff and untgz have their own Makefiles (untgz also Makefile.msc), and contrib/minizip has a plain Makefile and an Automake build (Makefile.am: libminizip.la, miniunzip, minizip); untgz and minizip's Makefile link ../../libz.a, so they need the configure build first",
    "platform makefiles are units too, rooted in their own folder although they are run from the zlib root (make -f win32/Makefile.gcc): msdos/ (five compilers, each declaring example.exe and minigzip.exe), win32/, amiga/, old/, old/os2/, watcom/ and nintendods/; the library names come from variables (ZLIB_LIB = zlib_$(MODEL).lib with MODEL=l or L, STATICLIB, SHAREDLIB, IMPLIB, OUTPUT)",
    "old/Makefile.riscos, old/os2/Makefile.os2 and old/descrip.mms still list gzio.c, a file that no longer exists: they cannot build this commit; make_vms.com is a DCL script that builds libz.olb, example and minigzip by commands, like configure, and is not a unit",
    "contrib/vstudio holds six Visual Studio projects per version: 30 MSBuild .vcxproj (vc10, vc11, vc12, vc14, vc17) and 6 older .vcproj (vc9); zlibvc builds the DLL zlibwapi, zlibstat the static library, miniunz, minizip and testzlibdll reference zlibvc (ProjectReference, or the solution's ProjectDependencies in vc9), testzlib compiles the sources itself",
    "contrib/ada/zlib.gpr (GNAT project) and contrib/dotzlib/DotZLib.build (NAnt) are build files with no unit kind; os400/ builds with a shell script (make.sh) on IBM i, where make is not standard",
    "contrib/dotzlib/DotZLib/DotZLib.csproj is a Visual Studio .NET 2003 project (VisualStudioProject XML, not MSBuild) that references nunit.framework through a HintPath on drive E: with no version; contrib/nuget/nuget.csproj uses the MSBuild SDK Microsoft.Build.NoTargets/3.5.6 to pack prebuilt native binaries and compiles no code",
    "Ada (contrib/ada), Pascal and Delphi bindings (contrib/pascal, contrib/delphi) and C++ wrappers (contrib/iostream*) are code that no listed build compiles",
    "amiga/Makefile.sas is an SAS/C makefile: Linguist names it SAS by its extension",
    "contrib/gcc_gvmat64/gvmat64.S switches to .intel_syntax noprefix: Assembly, not Unix Assembly",
    "os400/zlib.inc is an ILE RPG copy member, not a C include; Linguist has no candidate for it",
    "the cmake_minimum_required range 2.4.4...3.15.0 sets policies up to 3.15; CI picks compilers through a matrix (gcc, clang, cl, gcc-11) and installs Ninja on Windows",
    "no external dependency in the C builds"
  ]
